    "owner:2026-11-08 rebuild the specification by SPEC_STANDARD, starting with the data structures",
    "register:spec-workbench docs/INSTRUMENT_INVENTORY_20261108.md section 5.1 (935ca484)",
    "owner:2026-11-08 Q12 accepted: the active-project list is read from projects/active"
  ],
  "rationale": "The one home (SPEC_STANDARD 15.4) of every policy value that generated code reads: typed constants of one deterministic provider module, because the Factory data/code seam (SPEC_STANDARD 15.9) gives a generator an access signature and never a value, and an address or a value written in a note is not a path to code (SPEC_STANDARD 15.3.1). Placed on 2026-11-08 by the owner's decision to rebuild the specification by SPEC_STANDARD, starting with its data; the groups are those of the owner-checked register (spec-workbench docs/INSTRUMENT_INVENTORY_20261108.md section 5.1, D01-D30). Each value is the value the accepted decision named by source_refs already held, carried unchanged; nothing is decided here. Money (A9): MONEY_CURRENCY, MONEY_FRACTION_DIGITS and MONEY_ROUNDING were rules.money_policy leaves; WORK_BALANCE_LABEL_SIGNS gives every WorkBalanceLabel the sign of the balance it labels (1 positive, -1 negative, 0 zero). Registry (A6, A30): the request path and its two project segments, and the request timeout were config leaves; the path templates of config.registry_request_paths are split into a path and two segments, because a template is not data (SPEC_STANDARD 15.11). The timeout is a release value of one process, not a deployment knob, and so a constant (15.2 check 4), as are the two session lifetimes and the credential entropy (A30). Closed relations over State 1 enumerations are version 2 record_tuple tables keyed by the enumeration and total over its members, so a member added without its row stops the build (6.10 version 2): AUDIT_ACTION_SIGNIFICANCE classifies every AuditAction as a significant mutation or not (A13); CAPABILITY_SET_MEMBERS says of every CapabilitySet and Capability whether the set holds it (A2; the administrator set is the operator set together with administrator_additions, an operation the notes state); STAFF_STATUS_TRANSITIONS and PRINCIPAL_STATUS_TRANSITIONS say of every pair of statuses whether the transition is allowed (A3); IMPORT_OUTCOME_AUDIT gives every ImportOutcome its AuditResult and where its reason_code comes from (A13, A18); TRANSPORT_GUARD_STATUSES gives every refusal of the transport guard its HTTP status (A25); BOOTSTRAP_EXIT_CODES gives every outcome of the bootstrap command its exit code (A29). SUPPORTED_SNAPSHOT_CONTRACT_VERSIONS and SUPPORTED_OCR_CONTRACT_VERSIONS are the accepted contract versions (A7), a table of integers because 6.10 has no integer tuple. The transport values (A25) are the API prefix, the viewer entry and logout paths, the paths answered no-store, the no-store cache control, the fixed security headers, the labels of a transport log record in their order, and the health paths and status (A25, R0-11). PASSWORD_MIN_CODEPOINTS and PASSWORD_MAX_CODEPOINTS bound a password inclusively (A16); COMPLETION_PERCENT_MAX bounds a completion percent inclusively, whose lower bound is zero (A20). A cell of an enumeration column names a member; the member's home stays the enumeration. Values a deterministic backend reads stay in its IR (the viewer cookie, the binary delivery response).",
